From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: dsi: Meet the D-PHY clock lane minimums

The clock lane timings are derived from clk_hs_prepare, which truncates
to a single byte clock at low data rates. At the Minimal Phone MP01's
208 Mbit/s that gives a 38 ns TCLK-TRAIL and 192 ns of TCLK-PREPARE plus
TCLK-ZERO, short of the 60 ns and 300 ns the D-PHY specification asks
for. The MP01's bootloader and vendor kernel run that link with a zero
time of 8 and a trail time of 2 byte clocks.

Raise the trail and zero times to those minimums, which gives the same 8
and 2 there. Faster links already meet them and keep their timings: at
the Zinwa Q25's 652 Mbit/s the clock lane is still 5/20/5/10 byte clocks.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mtk_dsi.c
@@ -265,8 +265,12 @@
 
 	timing->clk_hs_prepare = 70 * data_rate_mhz / (8 * 1000);
 	timing->clk_hs_post = timing->clk_hs_prepare + 8;
-	timing->clk_hs_trail = timing->clk_hs_prepare;
-	timing->clk_hs_zero = timing->clk_hs_trail * 4;
+	/* D-PHY: TCLK-TRAIL >= 60 ns, TCLK-PREPARE + TCLK-ZERO >= 300 ns */
+	timing->clk_hs_trail = max(timing->clk_hs_prepare,
+				   DIV_ROUND_UP(60 * data_rate_mhz, 8 * 1000));
+	timing->clk_hs_zero = max(timing->clk_hs_trail * 4,
+				  DIV_ROUND_UP(300 * data_rate_mhz, 8 * 1000) -
+				  timing->clk_hs_prepare);
 	timing->clk_hs_exit = 2 * timing->clk_hs_trail;
 
 	timcon0 = FIELD_PREP(LPX, timing->lpx) |
-- 
2.47.0
